# Architecture Shape LLM Guide

## Purpose

Validate configured file, symbol, argument, import, and line-count shape rules.

## When To Run

- After editing imports.
- After adding functions, classes, or public arguments.
- Before finishing work that changed file structure.

## How To Read The Result

- Each violation names the rule, actual value, and configured limit.
- Zero on boolean-style rules means the behavior is not allowed.
- Import findings mean direct or joined imports should be preferred.
- Line and count findings usually indicate the code wants a smaller unit.

## Examples

- If a callable has too many arguments, introduce a value object or split the workflow.
- If a class has too many methods, separate responsibilities by ownership.
- If an import alias is flagged, import the named module or symbol directly.
- If joined imports are required, combine imports from the same source into one statement.

## Agent Tips

- Do not suppress shape findings with local exceptions.
- Follow configured import rules.
- Split behavior only where it improves ownership.
- Always rerun this command before final response.
